  "body": "Stage 15 hardens FIRST_OFFER success classification so backend state is advanced only after the marketplace exposes strong post-submit evidence.\n\nFinding:\n- after clicking the first-offer submit button, the worker historically treated navigation to any Vinted `/inbox/...` conversation as sufficient to mark the backend listing `NEGOTIATING/currentStep=1`;\n- verification that the conversation actually contained our submitted offer was only best-effort and happened after the backend state change;\n- that backend state is later used by the persistent guard/audit reconciliation as proof that the real action happened, so a redirect/UI race could create false positive proof.\n\nFix:\n- add `SubmittedOfferConfirmationVerifier`, which waits for Vinted's own-offer price element and requires its parsed value to exactly match the submitted price;\n- FIRST_OFFER now performs this strong confirmation before calling the backend listing update;\n- if confirmation is missing/unreadable/mismatched after the real submit click, the existing post-quota failure path keeps the quota consumed and persistent FIRST_OFFER guard unresolved, so no automatic retry/resend is possible;\n- normal own-offer status logging and optional text-message behavior remain unchanged after a confirmed backend update.\n\nVerification:\n- the dedicated real Chromium smoke renders the same own-offer `data-testid`, proves Polish-formatted price parsing/confirmation succeeds, and proves a displayed-price mismatch fails closed with `do not retry automatically` semantics.\n\nScope: Playwright only. No backend schema/API, target filters, quota semantics, selectors, or scheduler cadence changes.",
